{"chunk_id": "c124b45df7b1", "text": "In the Kuru assembly, the gathered kings remain silent while Draupadi pleads for justice after being gambled away by Yudhishthira. Duryodhana exploits the silence, mockingly insisting that the Pandavas themselves must declare whether Yudhishthira is still their lord\u2014because if he is, then Draupadi is rightfully enslaved. The court reacts with uneasy approval and curiosity about how the Pandavas will respond. Bhima, seething with rage yet bound by loyalty and dharma to his elder brother, declares that if Yudhishthira considers himself lost, then the brothers are lost as well, though he vows terrible vengeance if freed to act. In the next exchange, Karna cruelly declares Draupadi a slave and urges her to choose another husband. The humiliation peaks when Duryodhana exposes his thigh to her, provoking Bhima\u2019s famous vow to shatter it in battle\u2014foreshadowing a pivotal act of revenge in the war.\nIn the dice-hall, Duryodhana taunts Draupadi and the Pandavas; Bhima vows vengeance after Karna insults her and Duryodhana exposes his thigh.\nThemes: humiliation of Draupadi, dharma and obedience, public silence and complicity, vengeance vows, Kaurava arrogance", "vector": [-0.023395786061882973, -0.02321624383330345, -0.01679414138197899, -0.011898151598870754, -0.020965054631233215, 0.02198706567287445, -0.020799322053790092, 0.0017919734818860888, -0.01745706796646118, -0.03599139302968979, 0.02211136557161808, 0.008839021436870098, 0.030135540291666985, 0.00872853398323059, -0.0055036721751093864, 0.02024688385426998, 0.04187486693263054, -0.00039598645525984466, 0.05104535073041916, -0.02093743346631527, -0.004288306459784508, -0.008403976447880268, -0.009819600731134415, 0.0247768834233284, -0.027414778247475624, 0.020661212503910065, 0.01492965966463089, -0.03256627172231674, 0.004630128387361765, -0.007734144106507301, -0.012726809829473495, 0.0010228750761598349, 0.0018558492884039879, -0.009094524197280407, -0.03684